      "text": "Cutting zone (chip formation):\n  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │   Uncut chip thickness (t₁)                                 │\n  │   ─────────────────────────────────────────────             │\n  │                              ╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱ chip flows       │\n  │                         ╱ PRIMARY         along tool face   │\n  │                    ╱ SHEAR ZONE ╲                           │\n  │               ╱   (45°±rake/2)  ╲                           │\n  │          ╱ (material shears here) ╲                         │\n  │      ─────────────────────────────╲──────                   │\n  │                        TOOL    ╲   Flank face               │\n  │                            Rake angle α                     │\n  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-MACHINING.md#012",
      "path": [
        "05-MACHINING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:metalworking:05-machining, git-history:metalworking:05-machining]",
        "canonical_path": "metalworking/05-MACHINING.md",
        "concepts": "[machining]",
        "current_path": "metalworking/05-MACHINING.md",
        "id": "maxim:metalworking:machining",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "metalworking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[machining]",
        "section": "metalworking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Machining",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "RAKE ANGLE (α): angle between tool face and perpendicular to cutting direction\n  Positive rake (tool face tilts toward workpiece direction):\n    → Lower cutting force; thinner chip; better surface finish\n    → Weaker cutting edge (sharper angle = less material behind edge)\n    → Used for: ductile materials (aluminum, copper, soft steel)\n  Negative rake:\n    → Higher cutting force; tougher edge (more material support)\n    → Used for: hard materials (hardened steel, ceramics) with ceramic/CBN tools\n    → Harder materials need stronger (more negative rake) tools"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-MACHINING.md#013",
      "path": [
        "05-MACHINING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:metalworking:05-machining, git-history:metalworking:05-machining]",
        "canonical_path": "metalworking/05-MACHINING.md",
        "concepts": "[machining]",
        "current_path": "metalworking/05-MACHINING.md",
        "id": "maxim:metalworking:machining",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "metalworking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[machining]",
        "section": "metalworking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Machining",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "RELIEF (clearance) ANGLE:\n  Angle between flank face and machined surface\n  Prevents tool heel from rubbing machined surface → must be positive\n  Too large: weak edge; Too small: rubbing → heat → tool failure"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-MACHINING.md#014",
      "path": [
        "05-MACHINING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:metalworking:05-machining, git-history:metalworking:05-machining]",
        "canonical_path": "metalworking/05-MACHINING.md",
